    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0228" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1635</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moser</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-26T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1918,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 20, <hi rendition="#italic">2</hi> p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d182-f1"
                    /> last sentence. Department has no objection to your obtaining evidence
                    regarding occurrences at Blagoveshchensk provided you can do so unofficially and
                    without implying any recognition of Far Eastern Committee or affording any
                    indication <pb facs="0229" n="139" xml:id="pg139"/> of prejudice on the part of
                    this Government against any particular elements in Russia. Department can not
                    authorize appointment of a delegate to sit with committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
